{
  "description": "The keyboard of a typing-drill (format v1): the US QWERTY layout, which is the standard in the Netherlands (US-International has the same keys). keys: every key id of the newKeys enum with its char without and with Shift, its finger (left-pinky to right-pinky, thumb for the space bar; pinky for Shift, which has a key on both sides) and its hand (both for the space bar and Shift). chars: every char a line may hold (! to ~ and the space) with its key and the side of the Shift that types it (always the other hand, null without Shift). deadKeySequences: on US-International these keys are dead keys and compose with the next letter (' and e give é); deadKeys lists which letters each one composes, cases what content:check finds in a line (index of the dead key). tools/content/typing.mjs and web/src/app/interactions/typing-drill/keyboard-layout.ts are both tested against these cases.",
